From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blockchain-Oracle <blockchainoracle.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:24:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wallet: report sync progress through a SyncObserver

`WalletCore::sync_to_block` prints straight to stdout and drives an
indicatif progress bar, so a GUI or an embedded module cannot show sync
progress (and gets terminal noise instead).

Add a `SyncObserver` trait with no-op default callbacks for sync start
(the block range), per-block progress, finish and informational messages,
plus `sync_to_block_with_observer` / `sync_to_latest_block_with_observer`.
The existing `sync_to_block` / `sync_to_latest_block` delegate to them
with `CliSyncObserver`, which reproduces the previous output exactly,
including the progress bar and the per-block "Stored persistent
accounts" line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
